Wow. Previously nothing of this magnitude has been encountered. Luckily=20
this crap is, afaik, invisible to normal users, because the pages are=20
linked to from anywhere (except the TitleIndex).

Based on the history of the spam pages the spammer(s) used many user=20
accounts, and the edits were spread over a period of over 32 hours at=20
least. Assuming bots have not found a way around the Google reCAPTCHA we=20
use in the registration webapp these are real human spammers.

Anyways, I'll turn on a bunch of other spam filtering services in Trac=20
today, then add a few more on Monday. I'll also get rid of this crap=20
after more spam filtering is in place.

I hope we can avoid the situation where all edits have to be made by=20
known-good people. Right now Wiki edits are disabled for everyone except=20
a select few.

